+Input probes
+============
+AdversarialAudit.lean imported Proof and constructed SortIntSeq values from
+the listed integer character codes. It evaluated, in order:
+
+1. isDigitC 47
+2. isDigitC 48
+3. isDigitC 57
+4. isDigitC 58
+5. validScan "1/2/3/4" from phase 0 and zero accumulators
+6. scanResult "1/2/3/4" (3 mod 8 is nonzero)
+7. validScan "1/5/5/1"
+8. scanResult "1/5/5/1" (5 mod 5 is zero)
+9. validScan after mutating the first slash to digit code 48
+10. validScan after mutating a required digit to code 65
+11. validScan with an empty first numerator
+12. validScan with a missing final digit
+13. validScan with an extra trailing slash
+14. validScan from invalid phase 4
+
+It also compiled four `by decide` proofs showing observational inequality
+between the candidate definitions and these counterfactual mutations:
+
+- constant-true isDigitC at code 47;
+- constant-true validScan on the slash-to-digit mutation;
+- constant-true scanResult on 1/2/3/4; and
+- constant-false scanResult on 1/5/5/1.
+
+Command
+=======
+lake env lean AdversarialAudit.lean
+
+Result (exit 0; exact #eval output)
+===================================
+false
+true
+true
+false
+true
+false
+true
+true
+false
+false
+false
+false
+false
+false
+
+Operational bridge source comparison
+====================================
+«.List», «.Map», ListItem: exact empty/singleton collection constructors.
+_Map_, «_|->_»: exact generated partial K map operations on the target's
+defined, pairwise-distinct key cases; getD only totalizes undefined cases.
+_andBool_, «_<Int_», «_<=Int_», «_==K_»: exact Bool/Int/structural-K tests.
+builtinsScope: exact 23 source bindings from semantics/core.k with root parent.
+isDigitC: exact source rule 48 <= code <= 57 from semantics/methods.k.
+validScan: exact nine-rule base/recurrence/owise definition from verification.k.
+scanResult: exact six-rule slash/digit recurrence and terminal positive modulo
+test; the total fallback is outside the validScan domain used by the target.
+simplifyLoopBody, simplifyReturn: selected generated definitions are unwrapped
+from the exact verification.k AST equations; the fallback cannot occur for
+these generated symbols.
+simplifyScope: exact eight local bindings and parent(0).
+
+The proof executes the loop by induction through concrete Rewrites
+constructors (candidateLoopSound), including separate digit assignment and
+slash branches, then executes the frozen return expression. It does not prove
+the equation merely by rewriting both sides to a convenient custom function.
+An independent search of generated Rewrite.lean found no constructor with a
+#loop source and scanResult destination and no occurrence of either protected
+domain rule ID; the two obligations are not available as circular rewrite
+constructors. The three VERIFICATION_KLEAN_EXPORT constructors only evaluate
+the exported definition helpers (scope, validScan, scanResult).
diff --git a/evidence/pid-namespace-shim.c b/evidence/pid-namespace-shim.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a685668c5092174cffd0f268f4b825c0ec9bd2c1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/evidence/pid-namespace-shim.c
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+#define _GNU_SOURCE
+
+#include <dlfcn.h>
+#include <stddef.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <sys/types.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
+
+typedef ssize_t (*readlink_fn)(const char *, char *, size_t);
+
+ssize_t readlink(const char *path, char *buffer, size_t size) {
+    static readlink_fn real_readlink;
+    const char *suffix;
+
+    if (real_readlink == NULL) {
+        real_readlink = (readlink_fn)dlsym(RTLD_NEXT, "readlink");
+    }
+    suffix = path == NULL ? NULL : strrchr(path, '/');
+    if (path != NULL
+        && strncmp(path, "/proc/", 6) == 0
+        && suffix != NULL
+        && strcmp(suffix, "/exe") == 0
+        && strcmp(path, "/proc/self/exe") != 0) {
+        path = "/proc/self/exe";
+    }
+    return real_readlink(path, buffer, size);
+}

