+Audit mode
+==========
+AUDIT_MODE=CLASSIFICATION_AND_PROOF
+/audit-input.json resolution.mode=CLASSIFICATION_AND_PROOF
+problem_id=144-simplify
+condition=kit-semantics
+semantics_mode=SUPPLIED_SEMANTICS
+
+Lean PID-namespace compatibility
+================================
+The sandbox shell reports a PID for which /proc/<pid>/exe is absent, while
+/proc/self/exe works. Lean 4.22 consults /proc/<getpid>/exe to find its
+installation. The audit therefore compiled evidence/pid-namespace-shim.c and
+used only this execution environment for Lean/Lake commands:
+
+  LD_PRELOAD=/tmp/audit-work/libreadlink-self.so
+  LAKE_HOME=/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0
+  LEAN_SYSROOT=/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0
+  PATH=/opt/runtimeverification-k/pyk/.venv/bin:/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
+
+The shim changes only readlink("/proc/<pid>/exe") to
+readlink("/proc/self/exe"). It does not alter Lean sources, declarations,
+toolchain contents, project files, proof terms, or command output.
+
+Principal commands
+==================
+1. Producer hashes and image provenance:
+   PYTHONPATH=/reference python <independent hashlib + tools.pipeline_contract.sha256_tree script>
+
+2. Rule reconstruction:
+   PYTHONPATH=/reference python -c 'from tools.k_rule_inventory import inventory_verification; ...'
+   Inputs: /reference/k-proof and /reference/lemma-discovery.json
+
+3. Required Stage 4 preflight:
+   PYTHONPATH=/reference python -c 'from tools.klean_preflight import check_generation; ...'
+   check_generation(
+     /reference/k-proof,
+     /reference/lemma-discovery.json,
+     /reference/klean-generation,
+     toolchain_lock=/reference/klean-toolchain.lock.json)
+
+4. Fresh proof project:
+   copy /candidate source project to /tmp/audit-work/lean-project
+   copy /reference/klean-generation/generated to /tmp/audit-work/lean-project/Base
+   cd /tmp/audit-work/lean-project
+   lake clean
+   lake build
+
+5. Axiom audit:
+   lake env lean AxiomAudit.lean
+   where AxiomAudit.lean contains:
+     import Proof
+     #print axioms Proof.final
+
+6. Adversarial bridge checks:
+   lake env lean AdversarialAudit.lean
+
+All successful Lean commands used the exact environment above. The pinned
+toolchain reports Lean 4.22.0, commit
+ba2cbbf09d4978f416e0ebd1fceeebc2c4138c05.
